{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-hodge-star-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-hodge-star-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the categorical Hodge star","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-hodge-star","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-frobenius-pairing"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-hodge-star-exists"],"tags":["existence","hodge-star"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalHodgeStar.exists","text":"categorical-hodge-star-exists.md","leanSource":"categorical-hodge-star-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:categorical-hodge-star-exists\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Existence of the categorical Hodge star</em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a <a href=\"#def:quantum-universe\">quantum universe</a> of dimension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> with volume form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{vol} \\in \\Omega^n(A)</code>. The <a href=\"#def:categorical-hodge-star\">categorical Hodge star</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star \\colon \\Omega^k(A) \\to \\Omega^{n-k}(A)</code> exists as a morphism in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> and satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star^2 = \\mathrm{id}</code>. Uniqueness is shown in <a href=\"#prop:categorical-hodge-star-unique\">uniqueness of categorical Hodge star</a>.</p>\n"}
